# DECISIONS.log — append-only ADRs

## ADR-0001: PixiJS (WebGL) over raw Canvas2D — 2026-08-07
See commit history. PixiJS v8 behind IRenderer; Canvas2D fallback possible.

## ADR-0002: Fixed 60Hz simulation, interpolated render — 2026-08-07
Accumulator loop, max 5 steps, backlog dropped after 250ms.

## ADR-0003: All content in JSON — 2026-08-07
`src/data/*.json` is the single source of truth for content.

## ADR-0004: Door mats as first-class data — 2026-08-07
Every building carries an explicit `door` point; AI may only target door mats.

## ADR-0005: Gesture-gated procedural audio bus — 2026-08-07
AudioBus unlocks on first gesture; SFX/music are pure schedule data.

## ADR-0006: Engine modules as pure logic where feasible — 2026-08-07
Camera, rng, save, loop tick, audio schedules are node-testable.

## ADR-0007: Visual ambience is renderer-owned — 2026-08-07
Cars, particles, sky entities advance with render dt, never touch sim state.

## ADR-0008: A* over a walkable cell grid, not steering — 2026-08-07
Context: prototype NPCs steered directly and jammed on buildings, needing
stuck-hacks. Decision: 0.5-cell walkable grid derived from building data,
A* for all NPC/seeker paths, plus a data-level gate (`doorMatWalkable`)
asserting every door is reachable. Stuck detection remains as a safety net.
Consequences: path validity provable in unit tests; doorway regression e2e
covers all 14 doors.

## ADR-0009: Seekers share the NPC pathfinder — 2026-08-07
Context: seekers in the prototype steered directly at the player and clipped
buildings. Decision: seekers repath via the same A* every 2s toward the
player's cell, falling back to collision-safe steering only when the player
stands on an unreachable cell.
Consequences: seekers arrive through doors like citizens; no new pathing
code to maintain.
